In vol1 example stacks, we have a simple linear regression with
different
specification on the error term: normal, double exponential, student
t,
respectively.  Besides, two two different prior specifications
a set of coefficients (independent and ridge regression).
So we have 6 different models.  Now, only the two using
student t error terms works most of the time (it could
run into error as well).  The other four run into error
immediately.  A typical one is

Exception: Error in function
stan::prob::normal_log<N4stan5agrad3varE>(N4stan5agrad3varE): Scale
parameter is inf:0, but must be > 0 !

Diagnostic information:
Throw location unknown (consider using BOOST_THROW_EXCEPTION)
Dynamic exception type:
boost::exception_detail::clone_impl<boost::exception_detail::error_info_injector<std::domain_error>
>
std::exception::what: Error in function

stan::prob::normal_log<N4stan5agrad3varE>(N4stan5agrad3varE): Scale
parameter is inf:0, but must be > 0 !

---
Jiqiang

